          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong ultraproduct
            construction is an important tool in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
            that permits us to produce a new structure from an infinite family of structures. The construction has a decidedly ‘algebraic’ flavor and hence occurs naturally in applications of model theory to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
          %p
            It is closely related via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C5%81o%C5%9B+ultraproduct+theorem"} Łoś ultraproduct theorem
            to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactness+theorem"} compactness theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in some first-order language and a family of structures such that any finite subset of formulas is modeled by all but a finite number of structures. Then an ultraproduct of those structures may be used to model the entire set
            = succeed "." do
